# open leaders

Currently open **lowercase top-level leader keys**:

- `<leader>m`
- `<leader>t`
- `<leader>v`

Open uppercase slots:

- `A B C G M O T V X Z`

Digits `0–9` are also open.

Your original `<C-b>` mapping is unchanged.

neovim keys to consider remapping

`<C-b>` - page backward; largely overlaps `<C-u>`

`<C-y>` - precise upward viewport scrolling

> will not remap or did remap

`<C-e>` - mark actions

`<C-f>` - fold actions

`<C-g>` - picker actions in Insert mode; toggle Flash search in Command-line mode

`<C-r>` - set mark

> rest

Z - backspace in normal mode - almost always use something else to delete stuff in normal mode

H & L - top / bottom of screen - rarely useful, prime home row keys

C & D - change/delete to end of line are redundant with `c$`/`d$`, but convenient

`-` - previous line at first nonblank is rarely useful

| - exact-column motion is mainly useful in macros and fixed-width text

: - will remap to register-replace
~ - single-character case toggle is less useful than the `g~` operator
X - exchange operator; default delete backward is redundant with `dh`

s - Flash; default `s` is redundant with `cl`; restore default `S`
m & M - will remap to "move"

- Unicode name/glyph completion.
- Rainbow/nested-delimiter coloring.
- quicker.nvim maybe, really i just want the edit feature but the ui is not as nice as native

neovim stuff

- crtl-h needs to be <BS> in picker / fzf
- plugin to run rg on project and show hits in quickfix
- project wide find/replace (or on all open files, or folder).
- nvim cannot have any alt binds. snacks explorer has them by default but they need to be remapped. will need to check any plugins for alt binds and remap

# mini.nvim

* = done and fully setup
+ = added and partially setup
y = yes, will use
n = no can't or won't use

