 Proposed keybind plan

 ┌──────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │ Module               │ Proposed mappings / behavior                                               │
 ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ mini.ai              │ Keep a/i and existing ae/ie whole-buffer object. Change next/last to aN,   │
 │                      │ iN, aL, iL so Neovim 0.12+ an/in remain available. Disable g[/g] edge      │
 │                      │ mappings so built-in tag navigation is preserved.                          │
 ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ Native commenting    │ Replaced mini.comment with Neovim’s built-in gc/gcc and preserved the      │
 │                      │ legacy \\ line/visual mappings.                                            │
 ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ mini.completion      │ Keep <C-Space>, <C-f>, and <C-b>. Disable default <A-Space> because TODO   │
 │                      │ prohibits Alt mappings.                                                    │
 ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ mini.keymap /        │ Integrate rather than letting snippets overwrite your current insert       │
 │ mini.snippets /      │ mappings: <C-j> completion-next → snippet-expand → pair-aware newline;     │
 │ mini.pairs           │ <C-k> completion-prev → snippet-prev → current split-line fallback; <C-l>  │
 │                      │ accept completion → snippet-next → cursor-right; <C-h> remains pair-aware  │
 │                      │ backspace; <C-c> stops a snippet session.                                  │
 ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ mini.move            │ No Alt mappings. Visual H/J/K/L move the selection. Normal <C--> moves the │
 │                      │ line down and <C-=> moves it up, preserving your old unimpaired mappings.  │
 │                      │ Disable normal horizontal line movement initially.                         │
 ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ Wansmer/treesj       │ Replace mini.splitjoin and use gS to toggle split/join.                     │
 ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ mini.surround        │ Switch from the currently active Mini defaults to legacy-compatible ys,    │
 │                      │ ds, and cs. Put extra Mini actions on <leader>zf, <leader>zF, and          │
 │                      │ <leader>zh. Keep visual s for Flash, so visual surround would use ys       │
 │                      │ rather than the old S.                                                     │
 ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ mini.bracketed       │ Enable buffer b, conflict x, diagnostic d, jump j, location l, quickfix q, │
 │                      │ and Tree-sitter node n. Comments use [\ / ]\ and [| / ]|. Disable file,   │
 │                      │ indent, oldfile, undo, window, and yank targets.                            │
 ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ mini.indentscope     │ Keep ii, ai, [i, and ]i.                                                   │
 ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ mini.bufremove       │ Keep <leader>w and <leader>W, matching the old vim-bbye mappings.          │
 ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ mini.sessions        │ Use <leader>xs to select/read                                              │
 └──────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# Neovim migration TODO

## Active work

### Formatting and linting

- [ ] Add project-aware formatter/linter detection.
  - The idea is to inject via chezmoi repo data what auto formatters to enable into nvim data dir
  - Only autoformat if in a .git repo in the allow list
  - Always autoformat using normal detection if not in a git repo

### Navigation parity

- [ ] Audit `vim-unimpaired` behavior against `mini.bracketed`, `mini.move`, and custom toggles.
  - Check argument, buffer, file, tag, quickfix, location, conflict, and jump navigation.
  - Check blank-line insertion and line-moving operations.
  - Check option toggles.
  - Restore only operations still used.

- [ ] Restore quickfix/location-list toggles.
  - Old behavior: `<Leader>xx` toggled quickfix; `<Leader>xl` toggled location list.
  - New pickers inspect lists but do not toggle native list windows.
  - Implement directly with built-in `copen`/`cclose` and `lopen`/`lclose` if still wanted.

### Editor behavior

- [ ] Make trailing-whitespace handling follow EditorConfig.
  - Verify native EditorConfig support for `trim_trailing_whitespace`.
  - Do not restore unconditional trim-on-save.
  - Keep `mini.trailspace` for visualization/manual trimming.

- [ ] Restore project-local spellfiles.
  - Detect `.spellfile.utf-8.add` beside the current file.
  - Restore `:Mklocalspell`.
  - Preserve the old `$VIM_LANG` override for `spelllang` if it is still used.
  - Keep spell disabled in terminal buffers.

- [ ] Verify Markdown frontmatter highlighting.
  - Test YAML frontmatter with Tree-sitter Markdown.
  - Add a minimal override only if highlighting is broken.

- [ ] Restore Unicode name/glyph completion.
  - Support finding a character by Unicode name and inserting the glyph.
  - Preserve the old name/glyph display toggle if it remains useful.

### Marks and symbols

- [x] Use Snacks for the marks picker and `guttermarks.nvim` for sign-column visualization, navigation, current-line toggles, and deletion.

- [ ] Decide whether a persistent symbol sidebar is needed.
  - First evaluate Snacks LSP symbols.
  - Check whether ctags-based symbols are still needed when no LSP is active.
  - If a sidebar is genuinely useful, evaluate Aerial as the Tagbar replacement.
  - Do not add another plugin solely for duplicate symbol search.

### Visual structure

- [ ] Add rainbow delimiters.
  - Evaluate `rainbow-delimiters.nvim`.
  - Preserve a global/buffer toggle consistent with existing `yo…`/`\o…` conventions.

- [ ] Validate the Tree-sitter folding workflow.
  - Test fold accuracy, performance, persistence, and fold text.
  - [x] Restore fold mappings and add `nvim-origami` for fold UX.
  - Keep native Tree-sitter folds unless a concrete gap justifies `nvim-ufo`.

### Language support

- [ ] Restore Clojure workflows not covered by `clojure_lsp`.
  - Restore Fireplace and Salve for REPL/project integration.
  - Restore structural sexp editing and its regular-people mappings.
  - Verify whether clojure-lsp already covers formatting and diagnostics.
  - Restore cljfmt, Eastwood, or async omni only where LSP does not replace them.

- [ ] Restore modern Haskell tooling.
  - Prefer Tree-sitter and Haskell Language Server over the old hdevtools/neco-ghc setup.
  - Add formatting or test integration only if needed.

- [ ] Restore VimTeX.

- [ ] Restore Hugo template and MJML filetype detection.
  - Detect Hugo templates in HTML and Markdown files.
  - Treat `*.mjml` as HTML unless dedicated MJML support is added.

## Decide later

- [ ] Decide whether an in-editor test runner is still useful.
  - Old workflow used `vim-test`, Neoterm, and `<Leader>r…` mappings.
  - Choose a modern runner only after identifying the tests that should run inside Neovim.

- [ ] Explore a picker-based replacement for Projectionist alternate-file navigation.
  - Prefer a Snacks/FZF picker source over restoring Projectionist.

- [ ] Consider restoring thesaurus lookup.
- [ ] Consider Ruby `ri` documentation lookup.
- [ ] Add Ruby Bundler integration only if needed.
- [ ] Add JavaScript/CSS Emmet expansion and automatic tag closing only if needed.
- [ ] Add Python Simpylfold only if needed.
- [ ] Restore PHP four-space filetype indentation only if needed.
- [ ] Consider Terraform tooling and completion.
- [ ] Consider API Blueprint, GraphQL, and Riot-specific support when those filetypes are used again.
- [ ] Decide whether to restore `vim-abolish` functionality.
  - Word coercions such as camelCase/snake_case transformations are not replaced by `substitute.nvim`.
  - Also check whether abbreviation and enhanced substitution commands were used.
- [ ] Decide whether to restore searching for the current visual selection with `*`/`#`.
  - The old config provided this through `vim-visual-star-search`; Neovim does not provide equivalent visual mappings by default.
- [ ] Decide whether a unified documentation lookup should replace `investigate.vim`.
  - Existing LSP, help, and man-page pickers cover parts of the workflow but not one combined lookup command.
- [ ] Review insert-mode fuzzy completion parity.
  - Old FZF mappings completed lines, paths, and dictionary words.
  - The new config has native path completion but no explicit fuzzy line or dictionary completion.
- [ ] Decide whether to restore the old LaTeX `$…$` pair rules.
  - `mini.pairs` replaces general Lexima behavior, but the old config added filetype-specific dollar-pair insertion, escape, and deletion.
- [ ] Decide whether `mini.pairs` needs a buffer-local enable/disable toggle.
  - The old `yoe` mapping toggled Lexima per buffer and Lexima was disabled for Clojure.
- [ ] Review Fugitive-only workflows before removing it permanently.
  - Main Git status, diff, log, commit, stage, and unstage workflows are covered.
  - Check whether Git-aware move, remove, edit, and blame commands still matter.

## Intentionally omitted / no action

- [x] Vim-repeat: rely on modern plugin repeat support.
- [x] Airline tabline: intentionally omitted.
- [x] Promptline/tmuxline: intentionally omitted.
- [x] Old clipboard mappings: intentional workflow changes.
- [x] Mason/LSP provisioning: tools are managed externally.
- [x] General Neoterm runner: intentionally omitted.
- [x] Node local-bin/NVM, pyenv, and rbenv PATH management: obsolete; manage these outside Neovim.
- [x] Changelog macro: obsolete.
- [x] Old terminal-mode escape/navigation mappings: no longer needed.
- [x] Old `'`/`` ` `` mark-jump swap: obsolete.

